IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aa-types`
IMPORT `aa-act`

-- TESTS — Apportionment Act 1928. Expected values are worked from the Act;
-- the working is beside each. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests — Apportionment Act 1928`

GIVEN kind      IS A `Kind of payment`
      state     IS A `State of the payment`
      amount    IS A NUMBER
      begins    IS A DATE
      ends      IS A DATE
      due       IS A DATE
      land      IS A BOOLEAN
      allowance IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Payment
`a payment of` kind `,` state `, of` amount `for` begins `to` ends `, due` due `, on land:` land `, allowances` allowance MEANS
    Payment WITH
        `kind`                                              IS kind
        `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS FALSE
        `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS FALSE
        `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS FALSE
        `state`                                             IS state
        `amount of the entire portion`                      IS amount
        `accrual period begins`                             IS begins
        `accrual period ends`                               IS ends
        `entire portion due on`                             IS due
        `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS land
        `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS allowance

-- Quarterly rent of $9,000 for 1 Jan - 1 Apr 2026 (90 days), due 1 Apr.
`the quarter's rent` MEANS `a payment of` `rent` `,` `continuing` `, of` 9000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` TRUE `, allowances` 0

§§ `s 3 — accruing from day to day`

-- The landlord dies on 1 Feb 2026: 31 of the 90 days have run (fork F1).
-- 9000 x 31 / 90 = 3100.
#ASSERT `the part of` `the quarter's rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS 3100
-- The whole period adds up to the entire portion, and none has accrued on day 0.
#ASSERT `the part of` `the quarter's rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT `the part of` `the quarter's rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 0
-- A cut-off outside the period is a question about a different portion.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the part of` `the quarter's rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2026 4 2)

-- An annuity (a salary, s 2) of $3,100 a month for January (31 days):
-- 10 days run by 11 January — 1000.
#ASSERT `the part of` (`a payment of` `annuity` `,` `continuing` `, of` 3100 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, on land:` FALSE `, allowances` 0) `accrued at` (YMD 2026 1 11) EQUALS 1000

-- A dividend of $36,500 declared for 2025 (1 Jan 2025 - 1 Jan 2026, 365 days),
-- paid 31 Mar 2026. s 2 deems it to accrue "by equal daily increment during
-- and within the period for or in respect of which [it] is declared". The
-- holder dies on 2 Jul 2025: 182 days run — 36500 x 182 / 365 = 18200.
`the 2025 dividend` MEANS `a payment of` `dividend` `,` `continuing` `, of` 36500 `for` (YMD 2025 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 3 31) `, on land:` FALSE `, allowances` 0
#ASSERT `the part of` `the 2025 dividend` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 7 2) EQUALS 18200

§§ `ss 2, 3, 6, 7 — what is apportionable`

#ASSERT     `apportionable under the Act` `the quarter's rent`
#ASSERT     `apportionable under the Act` `the 2025 dividend`
#ASSERT NOT `apportionable under the Act` (`a payment of` `a payment that is not periodical income` `,` `continuing` `, of` 5000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` FALSE `, allowances` 0)

`a return of capital` MEANS
    Payment WITH
        `kind`                                              IS `dividend`
        `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS TRUE
        `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS FALSE
        `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS FALSE
        `state`                                             IS `continuing`
        `amount of the entire portion`                      IS 10000
        `accrual period begins`                             IS YMD 2025 1 1
        `accrual period ends`                               IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `entire portion due on`                             IS YMD 2026 3 31
        `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS FALSE
        `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS 0
`an assurance annuity` MEANS
    Payment WITH
        `kind`                                              IS `annuity`
        `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS FALSE
        `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS TRUE
        `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS FALSE
        `state`                                             IS `determined by re-entry, death or otherwise`
        `amount of the entire portion`                      IS 12000
        `accrual period begins`                             IS YMD 2025 7 1
        `accrual period ends`                               IS YMD 2026 7 1
        `entire portion due on`                             IS YMD 2026 7 1
        `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS FALSE
        `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS 0
`a rent with no apportionment` MEANS
    Payment WITH
        `kind`                                              IS `rent`
        `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS FALSE
        `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS FALSE
        `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS TRUE
        `state`                                             IS `continuing`
        `amount of the entire portion`                      IS 9000
        `accrual period begins`                             IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `accrual period ends`                               IS YMD 2026 4 1
        `entire portion due on`                             IS YMD 2026 4 1
        `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS TRUE
        `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS 0

#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `a return of capital` `at` (YMD 2025 7 2) EQUALS `not apportionable: a return or reimbursement of capital (s 2)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `an assurance annuity` `at` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `not apportionable: an annual sum under a policy of assurance (s 6)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `a rent with no apportionment` `at` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS `not apportionable: apportionment expressly excluded (s 7)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` (`a payment of` `a payment that is not periodical income` `,` `continuing` `, of` 5000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` FALSE `, allowances` 0) `at` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS `not apportionable: not periodical income within s 3`

§§ `s 4 — when the apportioned part is payable`

-- (a) continuing: when the entire portion becomes due, and not before.
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `the quarter's rent` `at` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS `apportioned` 3100 (YMD 2026 4 1) "s 4(a): when the entire portion becomes due and payable, and not before"
#ASSERT NOT `the apportioned part of` `the quarter's rent` `is payable on` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT     `the apportioned part of` `the quarter's rent` `is payable on` (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- (b) determined by re-entry on 2 Mar 2026 (60 days run): 6000, payable on
-- 1 Apr, when the next entire portion would have been payable.
`the rent determined by re-entry` MEANS `a payment of` `rent` `,` `determined by re-entry, death or otherwise` `, of` 9000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` TRUE `, allowances` 0
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `the rent determined by re-entry` `at` (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS `apportioned` 6000 (YMD 2026 4 1) "s 4(b): when the next entire portion would have been payable, and not before"

§§ `s 5 — remedies`

-- (1) "allowing proportionate parts of all just allowances": $900 of
-- allowances on the whole $9,000 portion; 31/90 of them, $310, comes off the
-- $3,100 accrued — $2,790.
#ASSERT `the recoverable part of` (`a payment of` `rent` `,` `continuing` `, of` 9000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` TRUE `, allowances` 900) `accrued at` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS 2790
#ASSERT     `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `the person entitled`
#ASSERT     `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `an executor, administrator or assign of the person entitled`
#ASSERT     `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `an executor, administrator or assign of a person whose interest determined with their death`
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `someone else`
-- (2) continuing rent charged on land: not from the tenant or the land, but
-- by suit against whoever receives the entire rent.
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `the quarter's rent` EQUALS `by suit against the person entitled to the entire rent, not against the tenant or the land`
-- A dividend: the ordinary remedies of s 5(1).
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `the 2025 dividend` EQUALS `the same remedies as for the entire portion`
-- Rent on land that has determined: still s 5(2), "an entire or continuing
-- rent" (fork F2 as revised after the independent pass; this assertion
-- expected s 5(1) under the first reading).
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `the rent determined by re-entry` EQUALS `by suit against the person entitled to the entire rent, not against the tenant or the land`
-- Rent not charged on land: s 5(1).
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` (`a payment of` `rent` `,` `continuing` `, of` 9000 `for` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, due` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, on land:` FALSE `, allowances` 0) EQUALS `the same remedies as for the entire portion`
